2 · THE MEASURED EFFECT AGAINST THE MARGIN
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  ⛔ Read the margin above FIRST. It was computed without reference to the effect.

  |mean within-B gap| 4.0155  vs  margin 0.8881  ⇒ ✅ CLEARS
  the effect is 9.04 sigma-hat (2 required)

  ⚠️ This is the ORDERING's effect within B — it says the rank coupling carries
     information at the real head's ordering quality. ⛔ It is NOT a promotion
     statement about B against A: S6 #585's A-vs-B criterion is VOID (its potency
     control failed), and S5 #584 §2b shows B LOSING to A on CRPS by +8.52.

  233.6 s, CPU, R=200 couplings, zero GPU, nothing retrained.
